%% AstraNotes - Activity Diagram (FR-05 startup persistence)
%% Auto-create data directory on first launch. Load loop skips bad files with
%% an error logged. OSError translated to PersistenceError per SPR-02.

flowchart TD
    Start([python -m astranotes launches]) --> ResolveDir[Resolve data_dir from ASTRANOTES_DATA_DIR<br/>or default ~/.astranotes/notes]
    ResolveDir --> DirExists{data_dir exists?}

    DirExists -- no --> TryMkdir[mkdir parents=True, exist_ok=True]
    TryMkdir --> MkdirOk{mkdir succeeded?}
    MkdirOk -- no --> RaiseDir[Catch OSError, raise PersistenceError - SPR-02]
    RaiseDir --> SurfaceDir[CLI surfaces user-friendly message]
    SurfaceDir --> End([End])
    MkdirOk -- yes --> ListFiles

    DirExists -- yes --> ListFiles[Glob data_dir/*.json]
    ListFiles --> Empty{Any files?}
    Empty -- no --> ReturnEmpty[Return empty list, CLI shows 'No notes yet']
    ReturnEmpty --> End

    Empty -- yes --> Loop[For each *.json file]
    Loop --> ReadFile[Read file, json.loads payload]
    ReadFile --> Parsed{Read + parse + build Note ok?}
    Parsed -- no --> LogSkip[Log error, skip file - FR-05 corrupt-file rule]
    LogSkip --> Next
    Parsed -- yes --> AppendNote[Append Note to in-memory list]
    AppendNote --> Next[More files?]
    Next -- yes --> Loop
    Next -- no --> ReturnNotes[Return Notes list, CLI shows menu]
    ReturnNotes --> End
